---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
staticPages:
  - ""
  - "about/"
  - "achievements/"
  - "ghcup/"
  - "minimoot/"
  - "events/"
  - "photos/"
  - "materials/"
  - "contact/"
  - "privacy/"
  - "terms/"
  - "accessibility/"
---
{#- The detail pages are generated from the collections rather than listed by
   hand. A hand-maintained list goes stale the moment an exec adds anything
   through the CMS — and it did: the previous version of this file listed ten
   URLs on a domain the site had already moved off, and omitted every
   achievement page, every exec profile, and two whole sections.

   The origin comes from site.url for the same reason. It appears here, in
   robots.txt, and in the canonical/Open Graph tags, and those four must never
   disagree about where the site lives.

   This comment closes on the same line as the XML declaration below, and that
   is deliberate: the declaration has to be the very first byte of the file, and
   closing the comment on its own line leaves a newline ahead of it that makes
   strict parsers reject the whole sitemap. Nunjucks has no whitespace-trimming
   form of the comment close tag, so same-line is the only way to do it. #}<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for page in staticPages %}
  <url><loc>{{ site.url }}/{{ page }}</loc></url>
{%- endfor %}
{%- for item in collections.achievements %}
  <url><loc>{{ site.url }}/achievements/{{ item.fileSlug }}/</loc>{% if item.data.date %}<lastmod>{{ item.data.date | isoDate }}</lastmod>{% endif %}</url>
{%- endfor %}
{%- for member in collections.team %}
  <url><loc>{{ site.url }}/team/{{ member.fileSlug }}/</loc></url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
